// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_wmic_eventconsumer_creation.yml
// ID Sigma: ebef4391-1a81-4761-a40a-1db446c0e625
// Título: NewActiveScriptEventConsumer Creation Attempt via Wmic.EXE
// Descripción: Detects the attempt to create an ActiveScriptEventConsumer via WMIC.EXE.
An ActiveScriptEventConsumer is a built-in Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) class that
automatically executes a predefined script (in VBScript or JScript) whenever a specific system event occurs.
Adversaries often abuse ActiveScriptEventConsumer to maintain persistence on a compromised host by executing a malicious script whenever a specific event occurs.

// Fecha de creación: 2021-06-25
// Fecha de modificación: 2026-06-19
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: high
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_wmic_eventconsumer_creation.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wmic.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\WMIC.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ActiveScriptEventConsumer" and ProcessCommandLine contains " CREATE ")
